  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening teacher standards, competencies, and capacities for effective response and recovery from learning disruptions, fostering resilience in education and improving learning outcomes</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Teachers are the bedrock of ensuring universal access to and participation in quality education for all. Their significance lies not only in their fundamental role in nurturing students&apos; learning capabilities but also in their profound understanding of education systems&apos; inner workings and the implementation of educational policies. Yet, in numerous Caribbean Small Island Developing States (SIDS), the pursuit of quality education is impeded by a dire shortage of teachers. These regions grapple with the challenge of attracting and retaining qualified teaching personnel, rendering their education systems ill-equipped to support effective teaching in the classroom and teachers to strategically plan their professional development initiatives. This workplan aims to strengthen teacher standards, competencies, and capacities for effective response and recovery from learning disruptions, fostering resilience in education and improving learning outcomes.</narrative>
  </description>
